@startuml
' Phase 5 — Forge: planned infrastructure. Authored at phase start.
' Copy to summary.uml at phase end and edit to the as-built state.

title Phase 5 — Forge (planned)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-forge (Go; imports contracts, toolbox)" as forge {
  component "forge (types + capability interfaces + audit log)" as core
  component "fake (deterministic, in-memory, offline)" as fake
  component "template (process templates)" as template
  component "memsync (forge -> contracts)" as memsync
  component "lifecycle (phase orchestrator + human gate)" as lifecycle
  component "rpc (transport-agnostic handlers)" as rpc
}

package "aa-contracts" as contracts
package "docs/github-os/templates" as templates
package "aa-memory (Sink, via RPC later)" as memory

contracts --> memsync
templates --> template
core --> fake
fake --> lifecycle
template --> lifecycle
memsync --> lifecycle
fake --> rpc
lifecycle --> rpc
memory ..> memsync : Sink (deferred writer)

note right of fake
  ADR-P5-007: the fake is the
  reference implementation and
  the e2e substrate. No network.
end note

note bottom of lifecycle
  ADR-P5-003: merge is a distinct,
  human-gated operation. The phase
  branch name equals the folder name
  and the phase PR starts Draft.
end note

note bottom of memsync
  ADR-P5-006: deterministic mapping
  to contracts; the forge never writes
  canonical memory directly.
end note

@enduml
